 .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"345\"> \n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span> ? ? Extinguishing nonconductive.</span>\n</p>\n </td> </tr> <tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; height: 86.25pt;\"> <td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 86.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"179\"> \n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span>Class D</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n</a><!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=ES-PA style=\'mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin; mso-hansi-font-family:Calibri;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:ES-PA; mso-fareast-language:EN-US\'><span style=\'mso-spacerun:yes\'> ? </span>SHAPE \\* MERGEFORMAT <![endif]--><!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=ES-PA style=\'mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin; mso-hansi-font-family:Calibri;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\";mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:ES-PA; mso-fareast-language:EN-US\'><v:shape id=\"_x0000_i1028\" type=\"#_x0000_t75\" style=\'width:.85pt;height:.85pt\'> <v:imagedata croptop=\"-65520f\" cropbottom=\"65520f\"/> </v:shape><![endif]-->\n</p>\n </td> <td style=\"width: 155.25pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-left-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 86.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"311\"> \n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span>Fires involving metals combustible<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\"> ? </span>such as:</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span>Magnesium</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span>Titanium</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span>Zirconium</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span>Sodium</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span>Potassium.</span>\n</p>\n </td> <td style=\"width: 172.5pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-left-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 86.25pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"345\"> \n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span> ? ? No dis ? wearable agent that effectively controls all types of fires in combustible metals.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; margin: 0cm 3.0pt .0001pt 3.0pt;\">\n<span> ? Special extinguishing agents for fire control for each of the metals and are specifically identified for that metal.</span>\n</p>\n </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> \n</div>\n\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: 150%;\">\n<strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span>3.13<span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\"> ? ? ? ? </span>General</span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>The fire suppression is based on the disruption of one or more factors of the essential elements of the combustion process. ? The combustion flame may be extinguished by reducing the temperature, removing the fuel, oxygen, or by stopping the chemical chain reaction. ? If the fire is in its dormant stage, there are only three options for termination: reduction of temperature, fuel removal and dilution of oxygen.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>As we have seen, there are three key factors that must be present to initiate and sustain combustion, they are: fuel, oxygen (air or other oxidant) and Heat. Theoretically, according to what was seen, we note that it is possible to extinguish burning through suppression and any of the three elements, giving rise to the basic methods of extinction.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: 150%;\">\n<strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span>3.14<span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\"> ? ? ? ? </span>Suffocation effect systems: carbon dioxide (CO2) and foams.</span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>The foam may be produced by mixing a solution of aluminumsulfate with other sodium bicarbonate and adding a stabilizer. ? In laptops foam is produced by the reaction of the two mentioned solutions, resulting in an internal pressure resulting from carbon dioxide generation, capable of impelling the foam to a distance of seven (7) feet.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>Foam removes oxygen to form a layer which prevents the passage of air, and also cools somewhat. ? Is applied as a layer covering the surface of the burning liquid. However, in many cases, the fumes arising from burning substances pass through the foam layer, and if the concentration is sufficient, it will burn up.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n</a><!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=EN-US><span style=\'mso-spacerun:yes\'> ? </span>SHAPE \\* MERGEFORMAT <![endif]--> <!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=EN-US><v:shape id=\"_x0000_i1027\" type=\"#_x0000_t75\" style=\'width:.85pt; height:.85pt\'> <v:imagedata croptop=\"-65520f\" cropbottom=\"65520f\"/> </v:shape><![endif]-->\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: center; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n</a><!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=EN-US><span style=\'mso-spacerun:yes\'> ? </span>SHAPE \\* MERGEFORMAT <![endif]--> <!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=EN-US><v:shape id=\"_x0000_i1026\" type=\"#_x0000_t75\" style=\'width:.85pt; height:.85pt\'> <v:imagedata croptop=\"-65520f\" cropbottom=\"65520f\"/> </v:shape><![endif]-->\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: center; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span><img src=\"@@PLUGINFILE@@/image%20%289%29.png\"></span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>It is especially useful in extinguishing class B fires, and where the smothering effect of extinguishing agent is of great importance. ? Certain solvents (alcohols, acetone, etc.) rolled foam, which is not convenient to use it on fire of these substances. ? Being electrically conductive should never be used on Class C fires also is contraindicated in Class D. Fires</span>\n</p>\n\n</strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<strong><span>CARBON DIOXIDE CO2</span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>This gas can be stored under pressure in portable extinguishers and discharged through a special nozzle on the site where it is needed. ? The property of the carbon dioxide extinguisher is its smothering effect accompanied by a slight cooling. ? Do not use in confined or poorly ventilated areas, as the user can be subject to mechanical asphyxia due to lack of oxygen, it is suitable for Class B fires and Class C. Not suitable for other types of fire.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1; margin: 0cm 0cm .0001pt 9.0pt;\">\n</a><!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=EN-US><span style=\'mso-spacerun:yes\'> ? </span>SHAPE \\* MERGEFORMAT <![endif]--> <!-- [if mso & !supportInlineShapes & supportFields]><span lang=EN-US><v:shape id=\"_x0000_i1025\" type=\"#_x0000_t75\" style=\'width:.85pt; height:.85pt\'> <v:imagedata croptop=\"-65520f\" cropbottom=\"65520f\"/> </v:shape><![endif]-->\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1; margin: 0cm 0cm .0001pt 9.0pt;\">\n<img src=\"@@PLUGINFILE@@/image%20%2810%29.png\">\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: 150%;\">\n<strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span>3.15<span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\"> ? ? ? ? </span>Inhibitor effect systems: powders</span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<strong><span>DRY CHEMICAL</span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>The products are mixtures of finely pulverized combustible, such as Sodium Carbonate, Sodium Bicarbonate, Sodium Sulfate, Sodium Silicate, Bentonite, etc. ? Works by drowning as it applies attempting to form a layer on the burning material.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>In laptops the extinguishing agent is ejected by the pressure produced by a nitrogen capsule, located inside the fire extinguisher and which is broken at the time of use.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span><img src=\"@@PLUGINFILE@@/image%20%2811%29.png\"></span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>According to the composition of the mixture, the dry chemical is suitable for Class A, B fires, and C. No e suitable for Class D fires.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: 150%;\">\n<strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span>3.16<span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\"> ? ? ? ? </span>Cooling effects systems: sprinklers, spray pressure </span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\">\n<span>Automatic sprinkler systems are one of the most reliable means to control fires.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>The percentage of effectiveness of sprinkler systems has been excellent for over 100 years they have used. ? To better understand the potential of these systems is essential prior knowledge of its components and applications.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: 150%;\">\n<strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span>3.17<span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\"> ? ? ? ? </span>Breathing apparatus</span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n<span>It is a universal portable device for artificial respiration. ? It is a simple device used for resuscitation, for artificial ventilation of the lungs that facilitates breathing and forced compulsory or arbitrary power by the rescuer respiratory expiration.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.0pt; mso-outline-level: 1;\">\n</a><span>It requires no separate power source or special skills to use.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: 150%;\">\n<strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span>3.18<span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\"> ? ? ? ? </span>Smoke-free drills</span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>The use of self-contained breathing equipment d in bailouts.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>The support team is normally assigned to support the attack team when the latter is performing its tasks in a fire fighting operation. It is usually intended to provide extra manpower by helping the members of the attack team to get equipped and by fetching equipment and breathing apparatus. In the vicinity of the fire, the support team has to establish a staging area, which is a smoke free area that is protected from the fire. Supplies of, inter allia, hose nozzles, axes and spare cylinders for breathing apparatus should be brought to this area by the support team.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>Apart from the tasks mentioned above, also identifies the following:</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Providing first aid to injured persons.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Preparing lifeboats and life rafts for evacuation.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Recharging self-contained breathing apparatus cylinders.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Conducting security patrols.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Providing boundary cooling.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>In this part and in the others, communication is a key factor for success. Communication is not only established between the team leaders and the captain, but between the team members and the team leaders. Good flow of communication enables the involved elements to carry out their designated tasks according to the prevailing situation. Through communication, the team leaders are given reports of thesituation of the fire and the problems encountered from the fighters. Consequently, they are able to give proper guidance and instructions after they have conducted an assessment of the situation. Nowadays, certain breathing apparatus are equipped with a radio. Similarly, the team leaders provide enough information to the captain in order for him to assess the situation and provide instructions accordingly to the team leaders. </span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>The team leaders are responsible for providing support and maintenance of the resources at their disposal for maximum readiness. For the attack team, the team leader ? s role is to ensure that each team member knows his designated task and provides brief instruction to fill a possible gap. He also has to ensure that fire fighters are relieved and rested after expending a long effort. Before and during the operation, the team leader is responsible for ensuring that the fire fighters are properly equipped. A close cooperation with the support team is necessary to ensure efficiency in providing filled breathing apparatus and other support, such as boundary cooling to help the attack team.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>The fire fighters should provide enough information to the team leader in order for the latter to properly maintain the resources available. The equipment resources comprise:</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Self-contained breathing apparatus.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Trolley sets.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Distress signal units.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Guideropes.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Personal guideropes.</span>\n</p>\n\n</span><!--[endif]--><span>Lifelines</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>SOLAS Chapter II-2, Regulation 17, also mentions about the ? fireman ? s outfit ? that consists of:</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3;\">\n<!-- [if !supportLists]--><span><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">1.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> ? ? ? ? </span></span><!--[endif]--><span>Protective clothing of material to protect the skin from the heat radiatingfrom the fire and from burns and scalding by steam. The outer surface shall bewater-resistant.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3;\">\n<!-- [if !supportLists]--><span><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">2.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> ? ? ? ? </span></span><!--[endif]--><span>Boots and gloves of rubber or other electrically non-conducting material.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3;\">\n<!-- [if !supportLists]--><span><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">3.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> ? ? ? ? </span></span><!--[endif]--><span>A rigid helmet providing effective protection against impact.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3;\">\n<!-- [if !supportLists]--><span><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">4.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> ? ? ? ? </span></span><!--[endif]--><span>An electric safety lamp (hand lantern) of an approved type with a minimumburning period of 3 h.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3;\">\n<!-- [if !supportLists]--><span><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">5.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> ? ? ? ? </span></span><!--[endif]--><span>An axe to the satisfaction of the Administration.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt;\">\n<span>Directing the team</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt;\">\n<span>The team leaders cannot be involved directly in the fighting operation nor is he involved directly in the supporting task (Stranding, 1989). In any case, the team leader should get involved in a fire fighting operation or support tasks. He should provide concise and precise orders to his team. Basically, based on the directives of the captain and the assessment of the situation, the team leader issues commands to his team members. He has to make sure that the team members do not take improper initiatives that may endanger their lives or worsen the fire situation. However, based on the team leader ? s knowledge of the qualification of the team members, he can give them the opportunity torespond without his order, but a report should be given to the team leader afterwards about this action.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify;\">\n<span>The team leaders play an important role in the achievement of the fire emergency. Being the on scene command, the team leader can see the situation directly, assess its severity and report to the master on the bridge. He can suggest alternative actions if the action plan cannot be implemented, but he has to seek for approval from the captain. A lot of responsibility is in his hands as to maintain the resources at his disposal and to use them in an efficient way. An emergency response can never succeed if the team leaders do not respond efficiently to the emergency.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal;\">\n<strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span>3.19 Use of Breathing Apparatus </span></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>These devices are used primarily in two areas: in the work of fire crews and industrial uses. For fire fighting equipment, the design emphasizes the strength of the components to heat and fire on the cost of the use of materials with these features and others such as lightness, essential for these envelopes containing large quantities of material. In industrial applications we can find the mining, industry, petrochemicals and others, being intended to protect workers who have to work in hazardous atmospheres.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">\n<span><img src=\"@@PLUGINFILE@@/image%20%2812%29.png\"></span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">\n<span>A self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA) sometimes referred to as a compressed air breathing apparatus (CABA) or simply breathing apparatus (BA), is a device worn to provide breathable air in an atmosphere that is immediately dangerous to life or health. They are typically used in fire fighting and industry. The term self-contained means that the SCBA is not dependent on a remote supply of breathing gas (e.g., through a long hose). If designed for use under water, it is also known as a Scuba set (self-contained underwater breathing apparatus). When not used underwater, they are sometimes called industrial breathing sets. Unofficial names include air pack, air tank, oxygen cylinder or simply pack, which are mostly used in fire fighting.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\">\n<span><img src=\"@@PLUGINFILE@@/image%20%2813%29.png\"></span>\n</p>',NULL,'text',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:28',1),(10002,18,'Review and Assessment','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\"></strong>\n</p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">7. Review and Assessment ? </strong>\n</p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">Evaluation is a way of finding out if learning has taken place. It enables the assessor (instructor), to ascertain if the leaner has gained the required skills and knowledge needed at a given point towards a course or qualification.</strong>\n</p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">The purpose of evaluation is to:</strong>\n</p>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">Assist student leaning;</strong>\n</p>\n\n</li>\n\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">Identify student ? s strengths and weaknesses;</strong>\n</p>\n\n</li>\n\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">Asses the effectiveness of a particular instructional strategy;</strong>\n</p>\n\n</li>\n\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">Asses and improve the effectiveness of curriculum programs;</strong>\n</p>\n\n</li>\n\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">Asses and improve teaching effectiveness.</strong>\n</p>\n\n</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-acc076fe-7fff-2d86-b587-13355c0f6939\">Upon successful completion of the examination which is carried out during and at the end of the course, the trainee will be awarded relevant course completion certificate issued by the training center.</strong>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n\n<br>\n\n<br>\n\n</p>',NULL,'text',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(10010,8,'Review and Assessment','<p>\n<b>12. Evaluation</span></b></a><b></span></b>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nEvaluation is a way of finding out if learning has taken place. It enables the assessor (instructor), to ascertain if the leaner has gained the required skills and knowledge needed at a given point towards a course or qualification.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nThe purpose of evaluation is to:</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Assist student leaning;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Identify student ? s strengths and weaknesses;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Asses the effectiveness of a particular instructional strategy;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Asses and improve the effectiveness of curriculum programs;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Asses and improve teaching effectiveness.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nUpon successful completion of the examination which is carried out during and at the end of the course, the trainee will be awarded relevant course completion certificate issued by the training center.</span>\n</p>\n\n<br>',NULL,'text',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(10013,5,'Review and Assessment','<p>\n<b>6. Evaluation</span></b>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nEvaluation is a way of finding out if learning has taken place. It enables the assessor (instructor), to ascertain if the leaner has gained the required skills and knowledge needed at a given point towards a course or qualification.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nThe purpose of evaluation is to:</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Assist student leaning;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Identify student ? s strengths and weaknesses;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Asses the effectiveness of a particular instructional strategy;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Asses and improve the effectiveness of curriculum programs;</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\n-Asses and improve teaching effectiveness.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nUpon successful completion of the examination which is carried out during and at the end of the course, the trainee will be awarded relevant course completion certificate issued by the training center.</span>\n</p>\n\n<br>',NULL,'text',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(10014,4,'Review and Assessment','<p dir=\"ltr\">\n<a name=\"_Toc93574293\" style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(73, 80, 87); font-size: 0.9375rem;\"><b>13. Evaluation</span></b></a>\n<br>\n\n</p>\n\n<p>\nEvaluation is a way of finding out if learning has taken place. It enables the assessor (instructor), to ascertain if the leaner has gained the required skills and knowledge needed at a given point towards a course or qualification.</span>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nThe purpose of evaluation is to:</span>\n</p>\n\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n\n<li>\nAssist student leaning;</span>\n</li>\n\n<li>\nIdentify student ? s strengths and weaknesses;</span>\n</li>\n\n<li>\nAsses the effectiveness of a particular instructional strategy;</span>\n</li>\n\n<li>\nAsses and improve the effectiveness of curriculum programs;</span>\n</li>\n\n<li>\nAsses and improve teaching effectiveness.</span>\n</li>\n\n</ul>\n\n<p>\nUpon successful completion of the examination which is carried out during and at the end of the course, the trainee will be awarded relevant course completion certificate issued by the training center.</span>\n</p>\n\n<br>',NULL,'text',NULL,25000,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(20002,8,'Libro 1 Versi n Espa ol',NULL,NULL,'file',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(20003,18,'Module 1 - Introduction',NULL,NULL,'file',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(20004,18,'Module 2 - Accidents and Emergencies',NULL,NULL,'file',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(20005,18,'Module 3 - Safe Working Practices',NULL,NULL,'file',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(20006,18,'Module 4 - Shipboard Communication',NULL,NULL,'file',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(20007,18,'Module 5 - Teamwork, Team Building & Effective Human Relations',NULL,NULL,'file',NULL,32767,0,'2026-04-19 03:45:30',1),(20008,18,'